<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Entitlements for the SwiftUI DarkbloomApp main executable of the release
      Darkbloom.app (signed in .github/workflows/release-swift.yml).

      Deliberately DIFFERENT from the co-bundled provider CLI
      (provider-swift/entitlements.plist):

      - NO keychain-access-groups / application-identifier /
        aps-environment. Those are restricted entitlements whose runtime
        authorization depends on the bundle's embedded provisioning profile;
        they exist only for the CLI's persistent Secure Enclave key and APNs
        code identity. The GUI app keeps NO secrets in the keychain (provider
        auth tokens are files under ~/.darkbloom) and never registers for
        push, so granting them would widen profile coupling for no function.
        The release workflow asserts their absence on the signed app binary.
      - NO get-task-allow: blocks debugger attachment under Hardened Runtime.

      Network: the app polls the local provider endpoint (LocalEndpointInfo /
      daemon-state) and may reach the coordinator API, so it keeps the same
      client/server network entitlements the CLI carries. (Both are sandbox
      keys — no-ops without com.apple.security.app-sandbox — but they document
      the intended surface and keep notarization assessment unambiguous.)
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
